{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanMagnitudeLift","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanMagnitudeLift","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanMagnitudeLift.borromean_H9_near_miss","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanMagnitudeLift.borromean_H9_near_miss","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BorromeanMagnitudeLift.lean#L140-L149","doc":"**Order recovered, coefficient open (the scope-(a) summary).**  At the `H₉`\nlevel (`E₀ > 0`, `h ≠ 0`, derived coefficient `κ > 0`) the magnitude is strictly\npositive (sign derived, #4360) AND, given the derived numeric value `0.297`, it is\n*not* equal to `μ₃ = 0.4708`.  So the magnitude *order/sign* is recovered 0-fit\nwhile the exact closure `= μ₃` stays open — NEAR-MISS LEAD, not a closure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanMagnitudeLift.not_closed_at_H9","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanMagnitudeLift.not_closed_at_H9","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BorromeanMagnitudeLift.lean#L127-L138","doc":"**The `H₉` level does NOT close the A=3 magnitude (near-miss).**  The derived\n`H₉` cabled-Borromean magnitude is `v_{H₉} = 0.297` (probe, 0 fit) and the target\nis `μ₃ = 0.4708`; since `0.297 ≠ 0.4708`, closure fails at the `H₉` level.  This is\nthe honest near-miss: right sign, right order (`O(h⁴)`, `0.63× μ₃`), exact\ncoefficient identity **open**.  (Stated with the derived value as an explicit\nhypothesis so `μ₃` never sets any coefficient.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanMagnitudeLift.magnitude_closes_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanMagnitudeLift.magnitude_closes_iff","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BorromeanMagnitudeLift.lean#L124-L125","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanMagnitudeLift.MagnitudeCloses","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanMagnitudeLift.MagnitudeCloses","kind":"def","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BorromeanMagnitudeLift.lean#L118-L122","doc":"**Magnitude-closure predicate.**  The A=3 Δ_λ magnitude closes at a level with\ncoefficient `κ` iff its magnitude equals the target moment `μ₃`:\n`E₀ · h⁴ · κ = μ₃`.  This is a *coefficient* identity — the level (hence `κ`) is\nFIXED and derived, `μ₃` is the target; a `κ` tuned to satisfy it would be a FIT. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanMagnitudeLift.levelMagnitude_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanMagnitudeLift.levelMagnitude_pos","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BorromeanMagnitudeLift.lean#L107-L114","doc":"**Positive `O(h⁴)` magnitude.**  With `E₀ > 0`, `h ≠ 0`, and a positive\nlevel coefficient `κ > 0`, the level magnitude is strictly positive — the same\n`+` sign #4360 derived, at any Brunnian-order-suppressed level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanMagnitudeLift.levelMagnitude","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanMagnitudeLift.levelMagnitude","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BorromeanMagnitudeLift.lean#L103-L105","doc":"The physical magnitude at a level is `c₃^L = E₀ · D_L(h) = E₀ · h⁴ · κ_L`\n(the `κ` evaluated at the physical `h`, treated as the level's coefficient). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanMagnitudeLift.lift_is_coefficient_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanMagnitudeLift.lift_is_coefficient_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BorromeanMagnitudeLift.lean#L91-L101","doc":"**Order-invariance of a level lift.**  For two Brunnian-order-suppressed\nlevels with deficits `h⁴·κ₁ h` and `h⁴·κ₂ h`, the lift ratio is `κ₁ h / κ₂ h`:\nthe shared `h⁴` factor cancels.  A level lift therefore rescales the *coefficient*\nand **cannot change the leading `h`-order**.  (The measured `H₃→H₉` exponent stays\n`4.098`; the `~49×` lift lives entirely in `κ_{H₉}/κ_bare`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanMagnitudeLift.kappaBare_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanMagnitudeLift.kappaBare_pos","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BorromeanMagnitudeLift.lean#L83-L87","doc":"`κ_bare(h) > 0` for every real `h` (`3 + h² > 0`, `h² + 4 > 0`): the bare\nlevel's `h⁴`-coefficient never vanishes, so the deficit is a *positive* `O(h⁴)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanMagnitudeLift.kappaBare_zero_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanMagnitudeLift.kappaBare_zero_pos","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BorromeanMagnitudeLift.lean#L78-L81","doc":"The bare-`H₃` `h⁴`-coefficient at `h = 0` is `3/4 > 0`: the leading-order-4\ncoefficient is genuinely nonzero, so the bare deficit is exactly `O(h⁴)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanMagnitudeLift.bare_deficit_eq_brunnian","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanMagnitudeLift.bare_deficit_eq_brunnian","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BorromeanMagnitudeLift.lean#L71-L76","doc":"The bare-`H₃` deficit realises the `brunnianDeficit` shape with `κ = κ_bare`:\n`h⁴(3+h²)/(h²+4) = brunnianDeficit κ_bare h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanMagnitudeLift.kappaBare","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanMagnitudeLift.kappaBare","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BorromeanMagnitudeLift.lean#L67-L69","doc":"The bare-`H₃` Borromean `h⁴`-coefficient (from #4360's closed form\n`1 − τ_Borr = h⁴(3 + h²)/(h² + 4)`): `κ_bare(h) = (3 + h²)/(h² + 4)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanMagnitudeLift.brunnianDeficit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanMagnitudeLift.brunnianDeficit","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BorromeanMagnitudeLift.lean#L61-L65","doc":"A Brunnian (order-`h⁴`-suppressed) level deficit with `h⁴`-coefficient\nfunction `κ`: `D_L(h) = h⁴ · κ h`.  The leading order is exactly 4 whenever\n`κ 0 ≠ 0` — every 2-sub-link of a Brunnian object is trivial, so the `O(h)`,\n`O(h²)`, `O(h³)` parts vanish. ","signatureChunk":0}]}